{
  "@context": {
    "@base": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/",
    "m1": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M1_CoreConcepts.jsonld#",
    "m2": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M2_GenericConcepts.jsonld#",
    "m3": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld#",
    "cartography": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M1_extensions/cartography/M1_Cartography.jsonld#",
    "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
    "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
    "owl": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#",
    "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#",
    "dcterms": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
    "adms": "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#",
    "skos": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
  },
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@id": "m1:extension:cartography:Cartography_Domain",
      "@type": "owl:Ontology",
      "dcterms:title": "M1 Narratives - Cartography Domain",
      "dcterms:description": "Domain-specific facets for cartographic map projections. Declares the classification axes by which projections of the terrestrial globe are filed: the distortion property a projection preserves (Map/REVOI side) and the geometry of its graticule (Territory/Structure side). First M1-declared facets under the SC-3 m3:Facet mechanism.",
      "dcterms:creator": "Echopraxium with the collaboration of Claude AI",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-09-09",
      "owl:versionInfo": "1.5.0",
      "m3:ontologyType": {
        "@id": "m3:DomainExtension"
      },
      "m1:domain": "Cartography",
      "m1:parentLayers": {
        "M2": "M2_GenericConcepts.jsonld",
        "M3": [
          "M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld (m3:Facet mechanism)"
        ]
      },
      "m1:childInstances": {
        "M0_instances": [
          "M0_World2DProjection.jsonld"
        ]
      },
      "m3:changelog": [
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "1.5.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-10-22",
          "adms:versionNotes": "SC-5b (Michel, decision table 28/28 + 2026-10-14/15): subdomains become domain classes (rdfs:subClassOf); stored subdomain lists deleted — subdomains are inferred from rdfs:subClassOf. m1:subdomains deleted."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "1.4.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-10-12",
          "adms:versionNotes": "SC-5 Domain fusion (Michel, 2026-10-11/12): domains are classes rdfs:subClassOf m1:Domain, never individuals. m1:extension:cartography:Cartography created ⊑ m1:Domain; registry data moved onto m1:extension:cartography:Cartography. m2:KnowledgeField / m1:KnowledgeFieldGenericCombo are obsolete (declared nowhere); the KnowledgeField-only keys m2:knowledgeFieldRole, m2:derivedFrom (now rdfs:subClassOf) dropped; m2:qualifier text kept as skos:definition. Obsolete KnowledgeField vocabulary purged from the live text (Michel, 2026-10-12: there is no KnowledgeField any more, it is Domain). m2:knowledgeField (obsolete, declared nowhere) renamed m1:domain on 1 class(es): an owl:AnnotationProperty whose value is the IRI of the domain class."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "1.3.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-10-03",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-2 lot CTX-5 (WS-5 prerequisite). Removed the @context terms \"m3:eagle_eye\" and \"m3:sphinx_eye\": term names in the form of a compact IRI that do not map to their own expansion (JSON-LD 1.1 §4.1.2). rdflib ignored them (no IRI produced anywhere in the corpus), strict JSON-LD 1.1 processors (pyld) rejected the file, and if honoured they would have pointed to the wrong IRI (M3 defines its terms under M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld#eagle_eye:X). Graph unchanged (isomorphic to the previous version). Scoping: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-5/WS-5_M3M2_Instrumentation_Scoping.md §4."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "m1:extension:cartography:Cartography",
      "@type": "owl:Class",
      "rdfs:subClassOf": {
        "@id": "m1:Domain"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Cartography",
      "rdfs:comment": "Discipline of designing, producing and studying maps, including the mathematical projection of the curved Earth onto a plane",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-10-12",
      "dcterms:creator": "Echopraxium with the collaboration of Claude AI",
      "skos:definition": "Science and craft of representing the terrestrial globe (or parts of it) on a flat medium, governed by the unavoidable trade-off between preserved and distorted metric properties",
      "m1:relatedDomains": [
        {
          "@id": "m1:extension:geology:Geology"
        },
        {
          "@id": "m1:extension:optics:Optics"
        },
        {
          "@id": "m1:extension:physics:Physics"
        }
      ],
      "m1:instanceExamples": [
        "M0_World2DProjection"
      ],
      "m1:instanceCount": 1,
      "m1:note": "First domain to declare M1-level facets (cartography:DistortionProperty, cartography:GraticuleGeometry) under the SC-3 m3:Facet mechanism."
    },

    {
      "@id": "cartography:DistortionProperty",
      "@type": [
        "m3:Facet",
        "skos:ConceptScheme"
      ],
      "rdfs:label": "Distortion Property",
      "rdfs:comment": "DISTORTION-PROPERTY facet (Map / REVOI side): which metric invariant of the globe a projection chooses to preserve exactly, given that no projection can preserve all of them (Gauss's Theorema Egregium). Metier term: 'distortion property' (ITC Living Textbook) / 'metric property' (map-projections.net). Closed value-set of four (epistemic tetra-lemma). A conferred, contingent, Map-perspective classificatory role. Foci carry non-neutral (geopolitical) weight — see per-value comments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:distortionProperty.Conformal",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:DistortionProperty"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Conformal",
      "rdfs:comment": "Preserves local angles / shapes (and therefore bearings) exactly; areas inflate without bound toward the poles. Navigation heritage (rhumb lines are straight). Exemplar: Mercator."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:distortionProperty.EqualArea",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:DistortionProperty"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Equal-area",
      "rdfs:comment": "Preserves area exactly; local shapes are sheared. Politically championed (Arno Peters, 1970s) as a more equitable representation of the Global South. Exemplar: Gall-Peters, Mollweide."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:distortionProperty.Equidistant",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:DistortionProperty"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Equidistant",
      "rdfs:comment": "Preserves distance exactly along specific lines only (e.g. from the centre, or along the meridians) — never all distances at once. Exemplar: Azimuthal Equidistant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:distortionProperty.Compromise",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:DistortionProperty"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Compromise",
      "rdfs:comment": "Preserves no invariant exactly; distributes distortion to minimise overall visual error rather than zeroing any single one. Exemplar: Robinson, Winkel Tripel, Natural Earth."
    },

    {
      "@id": "cartography:GraticuleGeometry",
      "@type": [
        "m3:Facet",
        "skos:ConceptScheme"
      ],
      "rdfs:label": "Graticule Geometry",
      "rdfs:comment": "GRATICULE-GEOMETRY facet (Territory / Structure side): the shape of the meridian/parallel network (the graticule), i.e. the construction family of the projection. Modern rigorous classification 'by the shape of the graticule' (Lapaine & Francula, 2022), which extends cleanly beyond the classical and contested 'developable surface' criterion (that one covers only 3 families). A conferred classificatory role. Extensible value-set (Pseudoconic, Pseudoazimuthal, Polyconic, Circular… added as instances require)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:graticuleGeometry.Cylindrical",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:GraticuleGeometry"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Cylindrical",
      "rdfs:comment": "Straight rectangular graticule: vertical equidistant meridians, horizontal parallels, right angles everywhere. Exemplar: Mercator, Gall-Peters."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:graticuleGeometry.Conic",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:GraticuleGeometry"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Conic",
      "rdfs:comment": "Parallels as concentric arcs, meridians as a converging fan of radii. Exemplar: Albers Equal-area Conic, Lambert Conformal Conic."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:graticuleGeometry.Azimuthal",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:GraticuleGeometry"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Azimuthal",
      "rdfs:comment": "Polar-style graticule: parallels as concentric circles, meridians as straight radii from the centre. Exemplar: Azimuthal Equidistant, Stereographic."
    },
    {
      "@id": "cartography:graticuleGeometry.Pseudocylindrical",
      "@type": [
        "m3:FacetValue",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "m3:valueOf": {
        "@id": "cartography:GraticuleGeometry"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Pseudocylindrical",
      "rdfs:comment": "Straight horizontal parallels but curved meridians converging toward the poles. Exemplar: Mollweide, Robinson, Sinusoidal."
    }
  ]
}
